I worked each expected output by hand using the cost model for interval increments: a target increment vector b (with b_i ≡ needed shift mod M) costs sum of max(0, b_i − b_{i−1}) with b_0 = 0. I chose the first element greedily, then the next, and so on, respecting the budget K. Expected outputs were checked by hand, not by running a reference solution.

